धर्मन्|धर्म्मन्
(-dharman, = dharma at end of cpds., as in Skt., BR; note pratyakṣadharman pw 〔5.260〕; nature, character, characteristic: yathā bālapṛthagjanā na (WT with Ḱ om. na) paśyanti pratyakṣadharmā (but mss. ˚mān!) tathāgataḥ … asaṃpramoṣadharmā (mss. ˚māḥ) SP 〔318.11—12〕 (prose; the acc. could be construed, with an implied paśyati, but the last word is clearly meant as n. sg.); jātidharmāṇaḥ sattvān LV 〔226.19〕; pratyakṣadharmā bhagavāṃ Mv 〔i.9.7〕; vipariṇāmadharmāṇo (n. pl.) 〔31.13〕; pāpadharmā (n. sg.) 〔36.13〕; cyavanadharmā (n. sg.) Divy 〔193.22 f.〕, ready to fall (from heaven to a lower existence); kāladharmaṇā (saṃ)yukta- Divy 〔210.28〕; 〔258.23〕, dead; jātidharmāṇaḥ sattvā(ḥ) Av 〔i.240.8〕, creatures subject to birth: see also avinipāta-dh˚; common.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=279,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

