Dharmapradīpavikramajñānasiṃha (1st ed. misprinted Dharmapradāpa˚; corr. 2d. ed.), n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔297.11〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रदीपशिरिमेरु
Dharmapradīpaśirimeru, n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔259.8〕 (vs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रभ
Dharmaprabha,<BR>(1) n. of a Bodhisattva: Gv 〔3.16〕;<BR>(2) n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔284.20〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रभास
Dharmaprabhāsa, n. of a future Buddha (= Pūrṇa Maitrāyaṇīputra, by prediction): SP 〔201.12〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मप्रिय
Dharmapriya, n. of a gandharva king: Kv 〔2.21〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबलप्रभ
Dharmabalaprabha, n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔257.2〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबलश्रीकूट
Dharmabalaśrīkūṭa, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔311.14〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मबुद्धि
Dharmabuddhi, n. of an ancient king (= the Bodhisattva): Av 〔i.91.16〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभाणक|धर्मभाणकः|धर्म्मभाणक|धर्म्मभाणकः
dharma-bhāṇaka, sometimes written ˚naka, as LV 〔179.10〕; 〔432.11〕 (= Pali dhamma-bh˚, Childers, s.v. bhāṇako; not in PTSD), a preacher of the doctrine, religious preacher: SP 〔19.9〕; 〔227.5〕; 〔343.9〕; 〔402.5, 7, 9, 11〕; Mvy 〔2764〕; LV 〔179.10〕; 〔432.11, 18, 19—20〕; Suv 〔66.12〕; 〔112.8〕; RP 〔15.11〕; Kv 〔13.12〕; 〔27.17〕; 〔78.1〕; Bbh 〔175.15〕; Dbh 〔46.12〕; ˚ka-tvam, state or condition of …, Dbh 〔76.24〕; Gv 〔417.25〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभाणिन्
-dharmabhāṇin, adj. (*dharma-bhāṇa, exposition of the doctrine, plus -in; cf. prec.), in aprāpta-dharmabhāṇin (actually to be analyzed as a Bhvr. aprāpta-dharmabhāṇa plus -in), not having received an exposition of the doctrine: dhārmaśravaṇikasyāprāptadharmabhāṇinaḥ AsP 〔244.20〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मभास्करश्रीमेघ
Dharmabhāskaraśrīmegha, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔309.5〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममण्डलपटलमेघ
Dharmamaṇḍalapaṭalamegha, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔311.9〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममण्डलप्रभास
Dharmamaṇḍalaprabhāsa, n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔257.23〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममण्डलविबुद्धश्रीचन्द्र
Dharmamaṇḍalavibuddhaśrīcandra, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔311.11〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममण्डलश्रीशिखराभप्रभ
Dharmamaṇḍalaśrīśikharābhaprabha, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔312.5〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममति
Dharmamati, m.<BR>(1) n. of one of the sons of the Buddha Candrasūryapradīpa: SP 〔19.4〕;<BR>(2) n. of one of the four deities of the bodhi-tree: LV 〔401.22〕;<BR>(3) n. of a former Buddha: Sukh 〔6.16〕; of a Buddha, Gv 〔285.14〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममतिचन्द्रा
Dharmamaticandrā, n. of a queen: Gv 〔232.12〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममतिविनन्दितराज
Dharmamativinanditarāja, n. of a former Buddha: Sukh 〔6.3〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममुख
dharma-mukha, nt., entrance or introduction to the [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280-b" target="_blank">Page280-b</a>] doctrine or to religion, way of entering it; so correctly Burnouf on SP 〔53.5〕, introductions à la loi, confirmed by Tib. on LV 〔161.14〕 chos kyi sgo rnam, doors or entrances to the doctrine or to religion. They are usually said to be very numerous: dharmāmukhā (˚mā˚ m.c.) koṭisahasr' aneke prakāśayiṣyanti anāgate 'dhve SP 〔53.5〕 (vs); asaṃkhyeyāni dharmamukha-śatasahasrāṇi niścaranti sma LV 〔128.8〕 (as the alphabet is recited, religious dicta come forth); a formulaic list, beginning (akṣayavimokṣa)-saṃbhedaṃ nāma dharmamukha(ṃ) Gv 〔195.24〕; sarvadharmaśubhavyūhaṃ nāma dharmam˚ 〔196.3〕, and others in 〔196.5—6, 8, 11, 14, 17, 20〕, etc. (the names are pompous but unilluminating); (sarvaromamukhebhyo) vividhāni dharmamukhāni niścaramāṇāny aśrauṣīt Gv 〔515.5〕, foll. by: yad uta, bodhisattvaguṇavarṇa-mukhāni dānapāramitā-mukhāni etc. (the cpds. become longer and more embracing as they proceed); precisely four are listed in LV 〔182.5 ff.〕, (bodhisattvaḥ …) catvāri dharmamukhāny āmukhīkaroti sma … (6) yad idaṃ … catuḥsaṃgrahavastu-prayoga-nirhāraviśuddhiṃ ca nāma dharmamukhaṃ … (and three other even more complicated ones, showing no clear relation to the Gv lists; it seems clear that there was no standard or accepted list); (bodhisattvāḥ …) dharmamukhaiḥ saṃcoditavyā bhavanti LV 〔161.14〕, are to be instigated (to withdraw from the world) by (the utterance of) introductions to religion (such as those which then follow in verses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममुखिका
dharmamukhikā (to prec.; pejorative -ka?), an (unworthy, deceptive?) introduction to religious teaching: (Upanandena tan mahalladvayaṃ) ˚khikayā vyaṃsitam (q.v.) MSV 〔ii.102.12〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममुद्रा
dharma-mudrā, ‘seal’ of the doctrine: iya … ˚drā SP 〔92.13〕 (vs); also dharma-svabhāva-mudrā, ‘seal’ of the true nature of the doctrine: bhāṣiṣyate ˚drām SP 〔28.8〕 (vs); deśem' imāṃ ˚drām 〔47.8〕 (vs). Tib. renders literally, phyag rgya, and so Burnouf, le sceau; Kern, closing word of my law, fixed nature of the law, (unmistakable) stamp of the nature of the law; probably the last rendering comes close to what is meant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघध्वजप्रदीप
Dharmameghadhvajapradīpa, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔310.10〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघनगराभप्रदीपराज
Dharmameghanagarābhapradīparāja, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔314.9〕 (vs); = Dharmadhātunagarābhajñānapradīparāja (in prose), q.v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघनिर्घोषराज
Dharmameghanirghoṣarāja, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔297.4〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघविघुष्टकीर्तिराज
Dharmameghavighuṣṭakīrtirāja, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔311.8〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्ममेघा
dharmameghā, n. of the tenth Bodhisattva-bhūmi (in the usual list; cf. abhiṣeka, ˚ka-vatī): Mvy 〔895〕; Dharmas 〔64〕; Bbh 〔354.26〕; Laṅk 〔15.5〕; Dbh 〔5.10〕, etc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयशस्
Dharmayaśas, n. of the father of Bakula: Karmav 〔76.10〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मयोग
dharma-yoga (m.; in PTSD dhammayoga is recorded, s.v. yoga, only from AN 〔iii.355.6〕, where it is a Bhvr. adj., ˚gā bhikkhū), application to a religious doctrine, in īdṛśa-dharma-yoge LV 〔420.20〕 (here a heretical doctrine); see s.v. pravādī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरति
Dharmarati, n. of a son of Māra (favorable to the Bodhisattva): LV 〔313.9〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरत्नकुसुमश्रीमेघ
Dharmaratnakusumaśrīmegha, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔309.14〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज|धर्मराजः|धर्म्मराज|धर्म्मराजः
dharmarāja(n), (mgs. 1 and 2 = Pali dhammarāja),<BR>(1) king of the doctrine or religious, righteous king, ep. of Buddha: LV 〔214.13〕; 〔395.9〕; 〔426.19〕; 〔437.18〕; ˚ja-putra (= jina-putra etc., of disciples or Bodhisattvas) Mvy 〔1090〕;<BR>(2) lawful (or righteous) king, as standing epithet of a cakravartin (cf. Pali DN comm. 〔i.249.29〕, glossed dhammena rajjaṃ labhitvā rājā jāto ti): Mvy 〔3618〕; LV 〔14.3〕; 〔101.13〕;<BR>(3) n. of a former Buddha: Mv 〔i.138.2〕 (˚jaḥ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराजिका
dharmarājikā, once dhārm˚ (from dharmarājan 1), [<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281-a" target="_blank">Page281-a</a>] lit. (edifice) which belongs to (serves for relics of) the king of the doctrine (= Buddha); a stūpa. So correctly BR; Burnouf Intr. 〔370 n. 1 and 631〕 is uncertain; Divy 〔Index〕 wrongly royal edict on the law. The mg. seems clear from (caturaśīti-)dharmarājikā-sahasraṃ pratiṣṭhāpayeyam Divy 〔381.14〕, ˚sraṃ pratiṣṭhāpitam 18, 23, while in the same passage, describing the same performance, in verse, we read: cakre stūpānāṃ … sāśīti … sahasram 21. To my mind this settles the matter. Other occurrences, always with forms of pratiṣṭhāpayati, establishes, founds: Divy 〔379.22〕; 〔381.5〕; 〔402.19〕; 〔405.15, 16〕; 〔419.15〕; 〔429.13〕; 〔433.27〕; 〔434.1〕; also dhārmarājikā 〔368.28〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=280,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मराज्य
dharmarājya, nt. (˚rāja, mg. 1, plus -ya), Buddha-hood: (bodhisattvānāṃ …) aprāpte ˚jye Mv 〔i.148.1〕, while they have not yet become Buddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मरुचि
Dharmaruci,<BR>(1) (= Pali Dhammaruci) n. of a disciple of Śākyamuni: Mv 〔i.246.3, 6, 12〕 (later incarnation of Meghadatta, q.v.); Divy 〔236.2 ff.〕 (here a number of the same stories are told of him as in Pali); Divy chap. 18 is called Dharmarucy-avadāna, Divy 〔262.6〕;<BR>(2) n. of one of the four deities of the bodhi-tree: LV 〔401.21〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मलब्ध
Dharmalabdha, n. of a merchant (previous incarnation of Śākyamuni): Mv 〔iii.286.16 ff.〕; ˚dhasya sārthavāhasya jātakaṃ, colophon, 〔iii.300.9〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविकुर्वितवेगध्वजश्री
Dharmavikurvitavegadhvajaśrī, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔297.8〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविमाननिर्घोषराज
Dharmavimānanirghoṣarāja, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔422.21〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मविवर्धन
Dharmavivardhana, n. originally given to Aśokaʼs son, later called Kunāla, acc. to Divy 〔405.24, 26〕. Known to Chinese sources: Przyluski, Açoka, 〔106〕 etc. (see Index).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मवेष्टि
dharma-veṣṭi, see veṣṭi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशरीर
Dharmaśarīra(-sūtra), n. of a short work: Stönner, SBBA 1904 〔p. 1282, 1283 (line 5 of text)〕. Here printed entire; a list of Buddhist religious categories.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशिखरध्वजमेघ
Dharmaśikharadhvajamegha, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔311.6〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मशूर
Dharmaśūra, n. of a former Buddha: Mv 〔i.141.9〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मश्रवण
dharma-śravaṇa, nt. (= Pali dhammasavana), listening to the doctrine, attending sermons and religions recitations: Jm 〔162.8〕 etc. Forms the basis of the next.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मश्रवणिक
dharmaśravaṇika, also dhārma-śrav˚ and ˚śrāv˚, adj. or subst. (from prec. form plus -ika; not recorded in Pali), listening (one who listens) to religious discourses: dharmaśrav˚ SP 〔283.2〕, all Nep. mss., ed. with Kashgar rec. dhārmaśrāv˚; Śikṣ 〔49.16〕; 〔355.10〕; Suv 〔104.2〕; 〔107.5〕; 〔128.16〕; dhārmaśrav˚ SP 〔20.13〕; Śikṣ 〔49.17〕 and 18 (thrice); 〔56.2〕; 〔197.16〕; 〔201.5〕; AsP 〔243.9〕; 〔244.20〕; dhārmaśrāv˚ SP 〔286.8〕 (and see above under 〔283.2〕).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मश्री
Dharmaśrī,<BR>(1) n. of a Bodhisattva: Gv 〔4.3〕;<BR>(2) n. of a Buddha: Gv 〔258.7〕 (vs; ˚śiriś ca, n. sg., m.c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

