dharmaskandha, m. (= Pali dhammakkhandha, on which see Childers, and cf. Kernʼs note in Transl. of SP, SBE 21, 〔p. 241〕), article or item of the doctrine, of which there are said (also in Pali) to be 84,000: Mvy 〔1417〕 (˚dhaḥ); dharmaskandhasahasrāṇi caturaśīti dhārayet SP 〔254.11〕 (vs; so read with most mss. and WT, as required by meter, contrary to note in KN, whose text is unmetrical).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

