धर्माकर
Dharmākara, n. of a monk (of old): Sukh 〔7.3 ff.〕; he became the Buddha Amitābha, 〔28.10〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्माकरमति
Dharmākaramati, n. of an author: Sādh 〔200.9〕; 〔417.7〕 (here called Madhyamaka-ruci).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धर्मादित्यज्ञानमण्डलप्रदीप
Dharmādityajñānamaṇḍalapradīpa, n. of a Tathāgata: Gv 〔309.7〕.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=BHS&page=281,2" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=bhs" target="_blank">Correction</a>

